<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Strymonians</h1><p class="st-meta">615 CE – 800 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Slavic tribe of the lower Strymon valley that joined the sieges of Thessalonica and long resisted Byzantine control.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Known mainly from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miracles-of-saint-demetrius">Miracles of Saint Demetrius</a> and Byzantine chronicles, the Strymonians settled along the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/struma">Strymon</a> (Struma) in the early 7th century and took part in the Slavic attacks on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki">Thessalonica</a> around 615.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They were a tribal people under local chiefs, farming the river valley and controlling routes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki">Thessalonica</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. In the 670s they again joined attacks on Thessalonica, and in 688 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-ii">Justinian II</a> campaigned against them and moved many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a> gradually brought the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/struma">Strymon</a> under control, creating the theme of Strymon by the 9th century, while the upper valley passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/first-bulgarian-empire">First Bulgarian Empire</a>. The tribe merged into the population of both.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 615 CE – 800 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Balkans and Hungary</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:71.94%;width:3.68%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>615 CE – 800 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Slavic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Slavic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a>, <a href="/countries/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, <a href="/countries/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Strymonitai, Strumyani</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=708&amp;focus=strymonians" aria-label="Strymonians on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5214 742 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Strymonians lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5534 998h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5534 998h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Greece. <a href="/atlas?year=708&amp;focus=strymonians">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

